  "findings": [
    "Continuing the projected parent with the revised recipe raises held-out math from 15/128 to 49/128 without KL and 48/128 with KL; replay-family correctness rises from 74/112 to 101/112 and 97/112.",
    "The corresponding stock arms also improve math and replay-family correctness, but lose fresh program answers and strict science-rubric passes.",
    "Adding replay-only forward KL shows no generation advantage overall in this single-seed pilot. Stock loses six replay-family answers versus CE alone; all six are in Python or sorting. Its item-resampled interval excludes zero, while family-cluster sensitivity reaches zero.",
    "Projected science stays 0/8 on the strict factual explanation rubric. This does not mean every answer lacks every relevant fact.",
    "A1 loses one net fresh program answer. A2 has no net program loss but loses the same regex case and gains another; it adds one repetition flag. No trained arm satisfies all descriptive test safeguards.",
    "The new A2 repetition flag is a 60-token, EOS-terminated water explanation repeated before an Answer line. It is not an endless generation or failed termination.",
    "All trained arms complete 260/260 test answers; stock completes 242/260 and projected parent 259/260 under the fixed token caps."
  ],
  "case_audits": {
