    }
  },
  "limits": [
    "One training seed and one fixed endpoint. Intervals are exploratory and uncorrected for multiple comparisons.",
    "Math and replay tests use held-out instances of known task families, not novel-family generalization. Family-cluster sensitivity is reported separately.",
    "Program sets have only 6 dev and 12 test source groups, including simple tasks; science has 4 dev and 8 test items with no interval reported.",
    "Science uses every required proposition and no core factual contradictions; strict-rubric failures can include partially correct answers. Both original ratings and adjudications are retained.",
    "A0-to-A1 combines continued training, rank expansion and a revised curriculum. This round cannot isolate which curriculum change helps, nor directly compare against the old recipe at equal dose.",
    "A1-to-A2 and S1-to-S2 isolate the addition of replay-only forward KL. The projected and stock arms have different earlier training histories.",
    "All test endpoints were fixed before generation; no test-based checkpoint search, threshold adjustment or promotion occurred.",
    "Fresh program safeguards use net category correctness; historical program vetoes separately require no lost individual case.",
    "Generation evidence does not settle broad distribution retention or alternate allocation quality."
  ],
  "decision": "Keep the current projected parent as default. Preserve all candidate adapters for analysis; do not promote a candidate from these results.",
